b)	typical Maltese interjections and their usages;
c)	elision and contractions used in Maltese speech;
d)	basic conjunctions and other combining elements in Maltese;
e)	filler phrases used by native Maltese speakers to enhance naturalness. a)	better pronunciation and intonation;
b)	improved linguistic knowledge and competence;
c)	adaptability to a variety of communicative situations. a)	formulate fluent phrases in Maltese with regards to various topics requiring formal modes of speech;
b)	use intonation to transform statements into questions;
c)	apply notions acquired from the previous course and modules for a natural expression in Maltese;
d)	distinguish words and phrases with similar but not identical meanings;
